      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A combination of specifically detumescent and analgesic/antiphlogistic substances (Dolo Mobilat film tablets) was tested in a double-blind study against placebo. The active product brought about very good or good therapeutic results in approximately 78% of 50 patients suffering from distortions of joints and from painful inflammation and swelling of non-traumatic origin; the corresponding percentage obtained with the placebo was 34%. Separate evaluations of pain and swellings most relevant for their homogeneity in distortions of joints showed rates of 80% and 31%, respectively. These differences as to efficacy are highly significant (p less than 0.001). There were no symptoms of intolerance except some sporadic mild gastric complaints. In comparison with the experience made with analgesics and antiphlogistics in oral therapy the action and tolerance were judged as very good."},
